---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {skills,href} from '../data/profile';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ComplianceSection from '../components/ComplianceSection.astro';
---
<Layout title="About Mohamed Yousry">
  <section class="container page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT / MOHAMED YOUSRY</span><h1>About <span>Mohamed Yousry</span></h1><p>I’m an Embedded Software & Cybersecurity Engineer with 4+ years of professional embedded software experience, primarily in safety-critical medical devices.</p></section>
  <section class="container about-grid section"><div class="about-monogram" aria-hidden="true"><span>MY<span>.</span></span><div>SOFTWARE × HARDWARE<br/>SECURITY × RELIABILITY</div><Icon name="cpu" size={70}/></div><div class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">PROFESSIONAL BACKGROUND</span><h2>Mechanical engineering and embedded software</h2><p>My background in mechanical engineering gives me a useful perspective on embedded development: software exists inside a physical system, with timing, sensing, actuation, and safety constraints.</p><p>Since 2022, I’ve worked as a Senior Embedded Software Engineer at Ezz Steel · Ezzmedical. My professional work connects medical-device firmware, real-time control, hardware-backed cybersecurity, and software verification.</p><p>I develop Embedded C firmware on NXP Power Architecture and STM32 platforms. My technical areas include HSM / SHE services, cryptographic integration, secure boot and firmware updates, feedback control, brushless DC motor control, and requirements-based verification.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('experience/')}>View experience & education <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div></section>
  <section class="section systems-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING APPROACH</span><h2>System design, security, and verification</h2></div></div><div class="principles-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Consider the complete system</h3><p>Connect software behavior to hardware interfaces, physical dynamics, execution timing, and failure handling.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Make trust explicit</h3><p>Define authentication, key usage, validation, and service boundaries so security decisions can be understood and reviewed.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Build reviewable evidence</h3><p>Link implementation choices to requirements, tests, and lifecycle documentation.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">CAPABILITIES & CONTINUED LEARNING</span><h2>Technical skills and learning interests</h2></div></div><div class="skills-grid">{skills.map(s=><article><h3>{s.title}</h3><ul>{s.items.map(i=><li>{i}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div><p class="learning-note">Learning interests: <strong>Embedded Linux, Yocto, and C++.</strong> These are areas I’m exploring, separate from my established professional competencies.</p></section><ComplianceSection eyebrow="MEDICAL DEVICE COMPLIANCE"/><ContactBlock/>
</Layout>

